ve, not follows the auxiliary.","C":"Place **not after had** and keep **drunk**: they had not drunk.","D":"Perfect negatives do not add did; not follows the existing auxiliary."}}},{"id":"d3575b67-9649-5530-af20-55321183c578","topicSlug":"past-perfect","level":"B1","prompt":"Begin this past-perfect question: ____ they drunk the fruit juice before the inspection began?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Are"},{"id":"B","text":"Has"},{"id":"C","text":"Had"},{"id":"D","text":"Did"}],"answerId":"C","hint":"The first auxiliary moves before the subject; do not add a new auxiliary.","explanation":"Move **had** before they. The participle drunk remains after the subject.","keywords":["perfect-question"],"skill":"perfect-question","contextKey":"past-perfect-47","fingerprint":"e4065f49461cbf4d31a6313874b8497053988a096116e1dc5825f428d9a627b3","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-past-perfect"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["The first auxiliary moves before the subject; do not add a new auxiliary.","Move **had** before they. The participle drunk remains after the subject.","Choose **Had**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"Are would create a different structure, not the requested perfect.","B":"Has does not agree with they, and cannot form a past-perfect question.","C":"Move **had** before they. The participle drunk remains after the subject.","D":"Did would require a base verb and would not make this perfect question."}}},{"id":"0405e251-160e-5143-a203-1b7429bfdc85","topicSlug":"past-perfect","level":"B1","prompt":"Choose the participle for the past perfect: We had ____ the fruit juice before the inspection began. (drink)","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"drinking"},{"id":"B","text":"to drink"},{"id":"C","text":"been drinking"},{"id":"D","text":"drunk"}],"answerId":"D","hint":"Identify th