d**: they had not held.","B":"Perfect negatives do not add did; not follows the existing auxiliary.","C":"The -ing form needs been for a perfect continuous, which is not requested.","D":"In the standard finite negative, not follows the auxiliary."}}},{"id":"4199cdf7-9c79-549d-a385-c3cab22bce37","topicSlug":"past-perfect","level":"B1","prompt":"Begin this past-perfect question: ____ they held the door open before the inspection began?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Are"},{"id":"B","text":"Has"},{"id":"C","text":"Had"},{"id":"D","text":"Did"}],"answerId":"C","hint":"The first auxiliary moves before the subject; do not add a new auxiliary.","explanation":"Move **had** before they. The participle held remains after the subject.","keywords":["perfect-question"],"skill":"perfect-question","contextKey":"past-perfect-48","fingerprint":"46b5865841fd542334b405a2bfa3f1bdc89979d0e9dad9d329ef05b9acf3aaae","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-past-perfect"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["The first auxiliary moves before the subject; do not add a new auxiliary.","Move **had** before they. The participle held remains after the subject.","Choose **Had**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"Are would create a different structure, not the requested perfect.","B":"Has does not agree with they, and cannot form a past-perfect question.","C":"Move **had** before they. The participle held remains after the subject.","D":"Did would require a base verb and would not make this perfect question."}}},{"id":"4dc00e27-80eb-5f61-aa8a-14ff9fd6a3f7","topicSlug":"past-perfect","level":"B1","prompt":"Choose the participle for the past perfect: We had ____ the door open before the inspection began. (hold)","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"held"},{"id":"B","text":"holding"},{"id":"C","text":"to hold"},{"id":"D","text":"been holding"}],"answerId":"A","hint":"Identify the past participle, rather than choosing a word only because it looks past.","explanation":"The past participle of **hold** is **held**. It follows had in the requested perfect construction.","keywords":["perfect-participle"],"skill":"perfect-participle","contextKey":"past-perfect-48","fingerprint":"90f5b4b0a4c129b8e3d2bd49b93f14c3baba48b923cebd0c1b681fa28fee1779","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-past-perfect"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Identify the past participle, rather than choosing a word only because it looks past.","The past participle of **hold** is **held**. It follows had in the requested perfect construction.","Choose **held**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"The past participle of **hold** is **held**. It follows had in the requested perfect construction.","B":"This is the -ing form, not the past participle.","C":"This is the to-infinitive, not a past participle.","D":"This would make a perfect continuous construction, not perfect simple."}}},{"id":"da63ee54-12da-5738-a579-160bd1d77996","topicSlug":"past-perfect","level":"B1","prompt":"Use the past perfect: She ____ the meeting records before the inspection began.","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"had to keep"},{"id":"B","text":"had been keeping"},{"id":"C","text":"had kept"},{"id":"D","text":"had keeping"}],"answerId":"C","hint":"Find the past reference and use **have + past participle**, with the auxiliary in the appropriate tense.","explanation":"The requested past perfect needs **had + kept** with she. The reference is before the inspection began.","keywords":["perfect-affirmative"],"skill":"perfect-affirmative","contextKey":"past-perfect-49","fingerprint":"947d86873cb63d15b4b3bca5aeed7c40657e150884f6cb2f470b1364581fd1f9","source":"seed","pr